course: dictionary
lesson: 1839
title: One word, many meanings
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Some words have more than one meaning, and the words around them tell you which one is meant. Cochin is one of these. «The Cochin hen fluffed up her feathers and clucked at the children.» Hen and feathers are clues, so Cochin here is a bird.
explain: Now look at this sentence: «Black pepper came mostly from the Malabar coast of south-west India, around Calicut and Cochin.» The clues are India, coast and pepper, so Cochin must be a place. It is the old English name of Kochi, a port city where spices were traded.
explain: A capital letter is another clue. A word with a capital letter in the middle of a sentence is often a name of a place or a person, as in «Cochin (now Kochi)». When a word has more than one meaning, put each meaning into the sentence and see which one makes sense.
fact: A Cochin is a large, fluffy breed of chicken, with feathers growing down over its legs and feet.
fact: Cochin chickens were first brought to Britain from Asia in the 1800s.
fact: Cochin is the old English name for Kochi, a port city in the state of Kerala in south-west India.
fact: Kochi was famous for spices and fishing nets.
fact: Cochin China was an old French name for the southern part of Vietnam.
exercise: «The Cochin hen had feathers growing down over her feet.» What is a Cochin in this sentence? | A fishing net | A port city in India | *A large, fluffy breed of chicken | A spice from the Malabar coast
exercise: «Black pepper came mostly from the Malabar coast, around Calicut and Cochin.» What is Cochin in this sentence? | A fishing boat | A French name for part of Vietnam | A kind of spice | *A port city in south-west India
exercise: «Cochin (now Kochi)» tells you the modern name. Which word is the modern name? | *Kochi | Kerala | Calicut | Vietnam
test: What is Cochin China? | A port in Kerala | *An old French name for the southern part of Vietnam | A breed of chicken | A spice from Calicut
test: Which is true of Cochin chickens? | Their legs are bare and smooth | They were brought to Britain in the 1900s | *They have feathers growing down over their legs and feet | They are wild birds from Vietnam
exam: «Black pepper came mostly from the Malabar coast of south-west India, around Calicut and Cochin.» What does Cochin mean here? | *Cochin is a port city in south-west India | Cochin is a kind of fishing net | Cochin is a fluffy chicken | Cochin is a French name for Vietnam
